<!--
  presentation-intake-poll.plist.template -- rendered by install.sh's
  install_intake_poll_schedule() (FIX 61); install.sh replaces every
  <...> placeholder below before writing the rendered copy to
  ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.blackceo.presentation-intake-poll.plist
  (Mac) or registering the 5-minute openclaw cron (Linux/VPS).

  PLACEHOLDERS install_intake_poll_schedule() replaces:
    1. <POLL_SCRIPT_PATH>          -- absolute path to presentation-intake-poll.sh
    2. <LOG_PATH>                  -- where stdout/stderr should go
    3. <POLL_PATH>                 -- the PATH launchd must give the job
    4. <PRESENTATION_RUNS_DIR>     -- the run root the poller scans
    5. <PRESENTATION_NOTIFY_CMD>   -- the notify transport (may render EMPTY)

  WHY 3-5 EXIST (2026-09-06). launchd hands a job essentially NO environment.
  This template previously declared no EnvironmentVariables at all, so the
  rendered LaunchAgent gave the poller nothing -- and launcher.py's
  fail-closed notify gate refused every dispatch with
  AF-NOTIFY-UNCONFIGURED (5,948 consecutive refusals measured on the operator
  Mac) while PRESENTATION_NOTIFY_CMD was present and non-blank in all three
  of that box's env stores. Fixing only the rendered artifact would not have
  survived the next install; the template is the thing that had to change.

  <PRESENTATION_NOTIFY_CMD> MAY RENDER EMPTY and that is safe by design:
  presentation-intake-poll.sh now loads the box's env store itself
  (presentation_job/env_store.py) and its precedence is process-env-WINS on a
  NON-BLANK value only -- so an empty string here does not shadow the store,
  while a real value here does win. The plist and the store are belt and
  braces, in that order, and neither silently overrides the other.

  The poll runs on the same 5-minute cadence as the watchdog: it scans for
  intake interviews whose ledger says complete but whose engine was never
  launched, and dispatches the engine (acquiring working/.lease.json first,
  FIX 61's dispatch lease). See presentation-intake-poll.sh for the contract.

  Uninstall (Named Stop -- do not run unattended):
    launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.blackceo.presentation-intake-poll.plist
    rm ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.blackceo.presentation-intake-poll.plist

  Verify it is loaded:
    launchctl list | grep com.blackceo.presentation-intake-poll
-->
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.blackceo.presentation-intake-poll</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>&lt;POLL_SCRIPT_PATH&gt;</string>
    </array>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>&lt;POLL_PATH&gt;</string>
        <key>PRESENTATION_RUNS_DIR</key>
        <string>&lt;PRESENTATION_RUNS_DIR&gt;</string>
        <key>PRESENTATION_NOTIFY_CMD</key>
        <string>&lt;PRESENTATION_NOTIFY_CMD&gt;</string>
    </dict>
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>300</integer>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>&lt;LOG_PATH&gt;</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>&lt;LOG_PATH&gt;</string>
</dict>
</plist>
